Good. I can see the scene from the player's spawn area. The important thing is that the milestone rules use `coordinate_frame="spawn_relative"` which means the evaluator automatically converts spawn-relative offsets to absolute coords. So I just need to use the relative offsets from the scene commands.

Based on the scene design:
- **Red concrete pillar center**: spawn-relative [8, 0-3, 8] (the pillar is at ~8, ~0 to ~3, ~8)
- **Terracotta deposit**: spawn-relative [10, 0, 6] to [13, 2, 10]

